              "text": "yantra comes from the root √yam \"hold, restrain\" with the tool suffix -tra (CDIAL 10412): in the Rigveda it is a controlling device, a prop or a fetter, and later any contrivance or machine (MW). Punjabi jandrā \"padlock\" comes from it (CDIAL 10412)."
